{
  "file": "Latent",
  "page": 38,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        54.572994232177734,
        526.7301635742188,
        67.37299346923828
      ],
      "text": "On the basis of existing practice, albeit, in the absence of a direct comparison, the GDG judged that 9 months’",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        68.57299041748047,
        526.7123413085938,
        81.37299346923828
      ],
      "text": "isoniazid is an equivalent option to 6 months of isoniazid in countries with a low TB incidence and a strong",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        82.57299041748047,
        526.7291870117188,
        95.37299346923828
      ],
      "text": "health infrastructure. It noted, however, that 6 months’ isoniazid is preferable to 9 months from the point of",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        96.57299041748047,
        364.11712646484375,
        109.37299346923828
      ],
      "text": "view of feasibility, resource requirements and acceptability to patients.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        116.24297332763672,
        526.6251831054688,
        129.04296875
      ],
      "text": "The recommendation that people living with HIV should be given at least 36 months of daily isoniazid",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        130.24298095703125,
        526.6810913085938,
        143.04296875
      ],
      "text": "monotherapy is conditional, as continuous IPT depends on the epidemiology and transmission of TB, the",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        144.24298095703125,
        267.3450927734375,
        157.04296875
      ],
      "text": "health infrastructure and programme priorities.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        163.9129638671875,
        526.6500854492188,
        176.71295166015625
      ],
      "text": "The GDG agreed unanimously that the benefits of 3 months’ daily rifampicin plus isoniazid for infants and",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        177.9129638671875,
        526.6531372070312,
        190.71295166015625
      ],
      "text": "children < 15 years of age outweigh the harm, given its safety profile, the higher rate of completion as compared",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        191.9129638671875,
        526.67724609375,
        204.71295166015625
      ],
      "text": "with isoniazid monotherapy and the availability of child-friendly, fixed-dose combinations of rifampicin and",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        205.9129638671875,
        492.0322570800781,
        218.71295166015625
      ],
      "text": "isoniazid. The GDG therefore made a strong recommendation despite the low quality of the evidence.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        232.9224853515625,
        246.0229034423828,
        249.71849060058594
      ],
      "text": "Considerations for implementation",
      "font": "Whitney-MediumItalic",
      "size": 13.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        252.60980224609375,
        223.6615753173828,
        266.8218078613281
      ],
      "text": "Drug resistance and surveillance",
      "font": "Whitney-Medium",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        270.42340087890625,
        526.6583862304688,
        283.223388671875
      ],
      "text": "There is no evidence of a significant association between bacterial resistance to TB drugs and use of isoniazid",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        284.42340087890625,
        526.6552734375,
        297.223388671875
      ],
      "text": "or rifamycins for the treatment of LTBI  . Nonetheless, active TB disease must be excluded before TB  (58, 59)",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        212.7860870361328,
        298.3634033203125,
        252.6680908203125,
        311.29339599609375
      ],
      "text": "section 3",
      "font": "Whitney-Bold",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        298.42340087890625,
        526.6331787109375,
        311.223388671875
      ],
      "text": "preventive treatment is initiated ( ), and regular follow-up is required to ensure early identification",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        312.42340087890625,
        526.6950073242188,
        325.223388671875
      ],
      "text": "of people who develop active TB while receiving TB preventive treatment. National surveillance systems for",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        326.42340087890625,
        521.76416015625,
        339.223388671875
      ],
      "text": "resistance to TB drugs should be established in countries implementing programmatic management of LTBI.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        351.6177062988281,
        242.19224548339844,
        365.8297119140625
      ],
      "text": "Interactions with antiretroviral drugs",
      "font": "Whitney-Medium",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        369.4313049316406,
        526.6161499023438,
        382.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "Regimens containing rifampicin and rifapentine should be prescribed with caution to people living with HIV who",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        383.4313049316406,
        526.6162109375,
        396.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "are on ART because of potential drug–drug interactions. These regimens should not be administered to people",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        397.4313049316406,
        526.6913452148438,
        410.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "receiving protease inhibitors or nevirapine. The GDG noted that the 3-month regimen of weekly rifapentine",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        411.4313049316406,
        526.6550903320312,
        424.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "plus isoniazid can be administered to patients receiving efavirenz-based antiretroviral regimens without dose",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        425.4313049316406,
        526.6422729492188,
        438.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "adjustment, according to a study of pharmacokinetics  . Administration of rifapentine with raltegravir was  (60)",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        439.4313049316406,
        526.6583251953125,
        452.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "found to be safe and well tolerated  . Rifapentine-containing regimens should not be administered with  (61)",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        453.4313049316406,
        526.684326171875,
        466.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "dolutegravir until more information becomes available. The GDG stressed the urgent need for studies of the",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        467.4313049316406,
        526.71240234375,
        480.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "pharmacokinetics of the 3-month regimen of weekly rifapentine plus isoniazid concomitantly with other drugs,",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8660888671875,
        481.4313049316406,
        142.8110809326172,
        494.2312927246094
      ],
      "text": "particularly ART.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        506.62548828125,
        208.0955810546875,
        520.8374633789062
      ],
      "text": "Monitoring of adverse events",
      "font": "Whitney-Medium",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        524.439208984375,
        526.6682739257812,
        537.2391967773438
      ],
      "text": "As individuals who receive treatment for LTBI do not have active disease, their risk for adverse events during",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        538.439208984375,
        526.6453857421875,
        551.2391967773438
      ],
      "text": "treatment must be minimized. Adverse reactions have been associated with isoniazid (asymptomatic elevation",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        552.439208984375,
        526.6604614257812,
        565.2391967773438
      ],
      "text": "of serum liver enzyme concentrations, peripheral neuropathy and hepatotoxicity), rifampicin and rifapentine",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        566.439208984375,
        526.6774291992188,
        579.2391967773438
      ],
      "text": "(cutaneous reactions, hypersensitivity reactions, gastrointestinal intolerance and hepatotoxicity). While most",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        580.439208984375,
        526.7070922851562,
        593.2391967773438
      ],
      "text": "of these reactions are minor and occur rarely, specific attention should be paid to preventing drug-induced",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        594.439208984375,
        134.41519165039062,
        607.2391967773438
      ],
      "text": "hepatotoxicity.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        614.1091918945312,
        526.6875,
        626.9091796875
      ],
      "text": "Individuals receiving treatment for LTBI should be monitored routinely at monthly visits to health care providers,",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        628.1091918945312,
        526.627197265625,
        640.9091796875
      ],
      "text": "who should explain the disease process and the rationale of the treatment and emphasize the importance of",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        642.1091918945312,
        526.6704711914062,
        654.9091796875
      ],
      "text": "completing it. Patients receiving treatment should be advised to contact their health care provider at any",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        656.1091918945312,
        526.67236328125,
        668.9091796875
      ],
      "text": "time if they become aware of symptoms such as anorexia, nausea, vomiting, abdominal discomfort, persistent",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        670.1091918945312,
        526.662353515625,
        682.9091796875
      ],
      "text": "fatigue or weakness, dark-coloured urine, pale stools or jaundice. If a health care provider cannot be consulted",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        684.1091918945312,
        401.22021484375,
        696.9091796875
      ],
      "text": "at the onset of such symptoms, the patient should stop treatment immediately.",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        703.7791748046875,
        526.665283203125,
        716.5791625976562
      ],
      "text": "There is insufficient evidence to support testing of baseline liver function  . It is, however, strongly  (62)",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        717.7791748046875,
        526.6913452148438,
        730.5791625976562
      ],
      "text": "encouraged, where feasible, for individuals with the following risk factors: history of liver disease, regular use of",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        731.7791748046875,
        526.6403198242188,
        744.5791625976562
      ],
      "text": "alcohol, chronic liver disease, HIV infection, age > 35 years, pregnancy or in the immediate postpartum period",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        745.7791748046875,
        526.6173706054688,
        758.5791625976562
      ],
      "text": "(within 3 months of delivery). For individuals with abnormal baseline test results, sound clinical judgement is",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        759.7791748046875,
        526.6572875976562,
        772.5791625976562
      ],
      "text": "required to ensure that the benefit of TB preventive treatment outweighs the risks, and they should be tested",
      "font": "Whitney-Book",
      "size": 10.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        39.40829849243164,
        790.2608032226562,
        56.68830108642578,
        810.61279296875
      ],
      "text": "26",
      "font": "Whitney-Light",
      "size": 16.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        796.524658203125,
        458.3740539550781,
        805.5686645507812
      ],
      "text": "LATENT TUBERCULOSIS INFECTION: UPDATED AND CONSOLIDATED GUIDELINES FOR PROGRAMMATIC MANAGEMENT",
      "font": "Whitney-Medium",
      "size": 7.0,
      "type": "heading"
    }
  ]
}